def find_max_val(a, b, c):
    # Calculate the minimum of a, b, and c
    min_val = min(a, b, c)

    # If any of them is less than or equal to this minimum, set it as the result
    if min_val > (a % b) + (b % c):
        return c

    # Otherwise, find the maximum of (a - min_val) and (b - min_val)
    else:
        return max((a - min_val), (b - min_val))
```

